    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "ibHDT",
      "x": 4620,
      "y": 102504,
      "name": "Note · Chicago options",
      "width": 460,
      "height": 620,
      "content": "SITE IN THE DASHBOARD'S LANGUAGE (direction A)\nWarm paper / warm charcoal, serif headline, ink buttons, gold only as accent, light + dark from the same tokens.\n\n1 · Warm-graded painting\nKeeps our existing skyline art, toned to the palette and framed as one card. Cheapest: art already exists. Reads as 'editorial photo', not wallpaper.\n\n2 · Line-art skyline\nA thin ink drawing of the skyline along the bottom of the hero. Calmest, most Claude-like; scales to any size and works in both themes. Needs a final illustration (this one is a generated sketch).\n\n3 · Flag stars + photos\nChicago flag stripes + 4 red stars as a small mark above the headline, real photos of the city and UIC beside it. Most recognisably Chicago and the only one that shows real places. Needs real photos (stock here are placeholders — the 'campus' shot is not UIC).\n\nThese mix: e.g. the flag mark (3) works with 1 or 2."
    },
